WEBVTT

00:01:28.996 --> 00:01:32.746
In both cases, the speaker presents
their audience with a possible future

00:01:32.788 --> 00:01:36.788
and try to enlist their help
in avoiding or achieving it.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.788
But what makes for good
deliberative rhetoric,

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:42.204
besides the future tense?

00:01:42.246 --> 00:01:45.371
According to Aristotle,
there are three persuasive appeals:

00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:46.413
ethos,

00:01:46.454 --> 00:01:47.871
logos, and pathos.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:51.954
Ethos is how you convince your audience
about your credibility.

00:01:51.996 --> 00:01:57.704
Winston Churchill began his 1941 address
to the US Congress by declaring,

00:01:57.788 --> 00:02:01.246
“I have been in full harmony all my life
with the tides which have flowed